{"causes": ["The expansionist policies of the Neo-Assyrian Empire under Sennacherib created a direct military threat to Elamite sovereignty and its influence over Babylonia.", "The long-standing geopolitical rivalry between Elam and Assyria, frequently involving interventions in Babylonian succession disputes, necessitated strong Elamite leadership.", "Internal power dynamics within Elam, including dynastic succession and the need to maintain a strong front against external threats, elevated figures like Kutir-Nahhunte IV to kingship."], "effects": ["Kutir-Nahhunte IV's leadership in the Battle of Halule contributed to a costly stalemate for both Elam and Assyria, temporarily delaying Assyrian subjugation of Babylonia.", "His death in 691 BCE, following a period of intense conflict, further destabilized the Elamite monarchy and accelerated its eventual decline under Assyrian pressure.", "The sustained Elamite resistance under rulers like Kutir-Nahhunte IV ensured the ongoing militarization of the region and prolonged the Elamite-Assyrian wars for several more decades."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "kutir-nahhunte-iv", "sourceName": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "battle-of-halule", "targetName": "Battle of Halule", "context": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV led Elamite forces in a major confrontation against the Assyrian army at the Battle of Halule in 691 BCE."}, {"sourceSlug": "sennacherib", "sourceName": "Sennacherib", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "kutir-nahhunte-iv", "targetName": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV", "context": "Sennacherib's aggressive campaigns against Babylonia and Elam directly precipitated the rise and military actions of Kutir-Nahhunte IV."}, {"sourceSlug": "kutir-nahhunte-iv", "sourceName": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "susa-elam", "targetName": "Susa, Elam", "context": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV ruled the Elamite kingdom from its ancient capital, Susa, during his brief reign."}, {"sourceSlug": "neo-assyrian-empire", "sourceName": "Neo-Assyrian Empire", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "kutir-nahhunte-iv", "targetName": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV", "context": "The constant military threat and expansionist policies of the Neo-Assyrian Empire heavily influenced the strategic decisions and reign of Kutir-Nahhunte IV."}, {"sourceSlug": "kutir-nahhunte-iv", "sourceName": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "babylonian-kingdom", "targetName": "Babylonian Kingdom", "context": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV formed an alliance with the Babylonian Kingdom to resist the Neo-Assyrian Empire, notably at the Battle of Halule."}], "places": [{"name": "Susa, Elam", "role": "Capital City"}, {"name": "Halule, Mesopotamia", "role": "Major Battle Site"}, {"name": "Anshan, Elam", "role": "Traditional Heartland"}], "texts": [], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q885591"], "tags": ["Monarchs & Rulers", "political-systems", "empire-and-colonialism", "geopolitical-linkage"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 6, "significanceNarrative": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV played a significant regional role by leading Elamite resistance against the formidable Neo-Assyrian Empire, notably at the costly Battle of Halule in 691 BCE, which temporarily checked Assyrian expansion and prolonged Elamite independence.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-10T09:45:20Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#29082254110", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV (b. 800 BCE) was a economist or social scientist of the Classical era, an age of empires, philosophical inquiry, and foundational civilizations, active in Global. Known in the fields of monarchs & rulers.", "newValue": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV, who likely reigned as king of Elam briefly around 693–692 BCE, was a pivotal figure in the final century of Elamite independence, primarily known for his role in the protracted struggle against the Neo-Assyrian Empire. Born around 800 BCE and dying in 691 BCE, his tenure, though short, occurred at a critical juncture when Elam was a primary geopolitical rival to Assyria, frequently intervening in Babylonian affairs and defending its own territorial integrity. He operated from Susa, the ancient Elamite capital, navigating a complex web of alliances and hostilities that characterized the Mesopotamian political landscape of the early 7th century BCE.

His most notable engagement was his participation in the Battle of Halule in 691 BCE, a major confrontation where a coalition of Elamite, Babylonian, and other allied forces faced the formidable Assyrian army under Sennacherib. Although Assyrian records claim a decisive victory, the battle's outcome was likely more ambiguous, representing a costly stalemate for both sides. Kutir-Nahhunte IV, who succeeded his father Humban-immen, was instrumental in marshalling Elamite military resources and providing strategic leadership against Assyrian encroachment, particularly their campaigns aimed at subjugating Babylonia, which Elam considered within its sphere of influence.

The immediate consequence of Kutir-Nahhunte IV's reign and the Battle of Halule was a temporary check on Assyrian ambitions in the Mesopotamian lowlands, though it ultimately failed to reverse the tide of Assyrian dominance. His death in 691 BCE, possibly related to the aftermath of Halule or internal Elamite politics, further destabilized Elam, paving the way for a succession of short-lived rulers and accelerating the empire's decline. The ongoing conflict exhausted Elam's resources and ultimately contributed to its catastrophic destruction by Ashurbanipal decades later, marking the end of Elam as an independent political entity."}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-10T09:45:20Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#29082254110", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Classical era: flourishing of philosophical inquiry, imperial expansion, and codification of la", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "800 BCE"}, {"title": "Dynastic succession and sovereign authority traditions", "type": "Idea", "year": "800 BCE"}], "newValue": ["The expansionist policies of the Neo-Assyrian Empire under Sennacherib created a direct military threat to Elamite sovereignty and its influence over Babylonia.", "The long-standing geopolitical rivalry between Elam and Assyria, frequently involving interventions in Babylonian succession disputes, necessitated strong Elamite leadership.", "Internal power dynamics within Elam, including dynastic succession and the need to maintain a strong front against external threats, elevated figures like Kutir-Nahhunte IV to kingship."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-10T09:45:20Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#29082254110", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Established dynastic legacies and territorial boundaries", "type": "Idea", "year": "691 BCE"}, {"title": "Contributed to enduring intellectual and institutional frameworks shaping subsequent civilizati", "type": "Movement", "year": "691 BCE"}], "newValue": ["Kutir-Nahhunte IV's leadership in the Battle of Halule contributed to a costly stalemate for both Elam and Assyria, temporarily delaying Assyrian subjugation of Babylonia.", "His death in 691 BCE, following a period of intense conflict, further destabilized the Elamite monarchy and accelerated its eventual decline under Assyrian pressure.", "The sustained Elamite resistance under rulers like Kutir-Nahhunte IV ensured the ongoing militarization of the region and prolonged the Elamite-Assyrian wars for several more decades."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-10T09:45:20Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#29082254110", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "kutir-nahhunte-iv", "sourceName": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV", "verb": "RULES", "targetSlug": "field-221", "targetName": "Monarchs & Rulers", "context": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV: Sovereign authority in monarchs & rulers"}, {"sourceSlug": "kutir-nahhunte-iv", "sourceName": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "classical", "targetName": "Classical Era", "context": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV was active during the Classical era"}], "newValue": [{"sourceSlug": "kutir-nahhunte-iv", "sourceName": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "battle-of-halule", "targetName": "Battle of Halule", "context": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV led Elamite forces in a major confrontation against the Assyrian army at the Battle of Halule in 691 BCE."}, {"sourceSlug": "sennacherib", "sourceName": "Sennacherib", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "kutir-nahhunte-iv", "targetName": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV", "context": "Sennacherib's aggressive campaigns against Babylonia and Elam directly precipitated the rise and military actions of Kutir-Nahhunte IV."}, {"sourceSlug": "kutir-nahhunte-iv", "sourceName": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "susa-elam", "targetName": "Susa, Elam", "context": "Kutir-Nahhunte IV ruled the Elamite kingdom from its ancient capital, Susa, during his brief reign."}, {"sourceSlug"